From: Aurélien Pommel <aurelien.pommel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip: inno-usb2: report the cable once detection ends

The OTG state machine records vbus_attached on any pass, but sends the
extcon cable only when it changes. A plug bounces: a second bvalid irq
during charger detection finds VBUS with nothing to report yet, records
it, and the SDP found afterwards no longer counts as a change. The cable
is never reported and the gadget never binds until a replug that does not
bounce. Record the change only together with its report.

---
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c	2026-10-26 20:08:21
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c	2026-10-26 20:08:21
@@ -746,10 +746,14 @@
 			rphy->chg_type = POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_UNKNOWN;
 		}
 
-		if (rport->vbus_attached != vbus_attach) {
+		/*
+		 * Only once the change is reported: a bounce mid-detection would
+		 * mark VBUS seen, and the result found later never be sent.
+		 */
+		if (notify_charger && rport->vbus_attached != vbus_attach) {
 			rport->vbus_attached = vbus_attach;
 
-			if (notify_charger && rphy->edev) {
+			if (rphy->edev) {
 				extcon_set_state_sync(rphy->edev,
 							cable, vbus_attach);
 				if (cable == EXTCON_CHG_USB_SDP)
